Prove the routine works for another period — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Contract
Use supplied standalone normalization starter. Run October twice into different new folders; compare business records. No code changes or stale September outputs.
Task
The same preparation routine must process October without code changes or stale September output.
Actions
	1	Use your prior routine or the supplied standalone reference script; review its period contract.
	2	Run October with --period 2026-10 into a new directory.
	3	Verify three accepted and two rejected rows and explain the two distinct period exceptions.
	4	Repeat the same input into a second new directory and compare output contents, ignoring only documented run metadata.
	5	Confirm no September outputs were reused and no code was edited to change period.
Output
Two commands; per-run counts; wrong-period/invalid-period reasons; comparison of accepted outputs; input-preservation note.
Supplied local practice files
	•	normalize.py
	•	october.csv
	•	september.csv
Keep these files together. Scripts take explicit paths; choose new output folders. Use a plain text editor to inspect source before running. Browser prototypes open locally; do not deploy them.
